From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/arm64: huawei-gaokun-ec: validate UCSI ACK port

GAOKUN_UCSI_NO_PORT_UPDATE is -1. Computing the ACK mask before checking
this sentinel executes a negative shift, even though the mask is then
replaced by zero. An idle sideband ACK triggered the following on Gaokun3:

  UBSAN: shift-out-of-bounds in huawei-gaokun-ec.c
  shift exponent -1 is negative
  gaokun_ec_ucsi_pan_ack
  gaokun_ucsi_sync_worker

Initialize the empty ACK to zero and only shift after validating the port
fits the one-byte ACK field. Reject other invalid values without EC I/O.
Keep transport errors and the no-update ACK behavior unchanged.

Signed-off-by: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
--- a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
@@ -459,10 +459,13 @@ int gaokun_ec_ucsi_pan_ack(struct gaokun_ec *ec, int port_id)
 {
 	u8 ec_req[] = MKREQ(0x03, UCSI_REG_WRITE, 1);
-	u8 data = 1 << port_id;
+	u8 data = 0;
 
-	if (port_id == GAOKUN_UCSI_NO_PORT_UPDATE)
-		data = 0;
+	if (port_id != GAOKUN_UCSI_NO_PORT_UPDATE) {
+		if (port_id < 0 || port_id >= 8)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		data = 1U << port_id;
+	}
 
 	refill_req_byte(ec_req, &data);
 
 	return gaokun_ec_write(ec, ec_req);
-- 
